      "output_preview": "## Database Layer — Complete\n\nCreated the full `team-test/database/` package with four production-ready files:\n\n### Files Created\n\n1. **`team-test/database/__init__.py`**  \n   Package init that re-exports `Base`, `engine`, `get_db`, `SessionLocal`, `User`, and `Project` for convenient top-level imports.\n\n2. **`team-test/database/connection.py`**  \n   - `DATABASE_URL` driven by `DATABASE_URL` env var (defaults to `sqlite:///./team_test.db`)  \n   - SQLite `check_same_thread=False` guard for FastAPI compatibility  \n   - SQLAlchemy 2.0-style `DeclarativeBase` subclass (`Base`)  \n   - `SessionLocal` sessionmaker (autocommit=False, autoflush=False)  \n   - `get_db()` generator dependency for FastAPI `Depends()`  \n   - `init_db()` helper that imports models then calls `Base.metadata.create_all()`\n\n3. **`team-test/database/models.py`**  \n   - `User` ORM model: `id`, `username` (unique), `email` (unique), `full_name`, `is_active`, `hashed_password`, `created_at`, `updated_at`; one-to-many relationship to `Project` with `cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\"`  \n   - `Project` ORM model: `id`, `name`, `description`, `is_active`, `owner_id` (FK → users.id with `ondelete=\"CASCADE\"`), `created_at`, `updated_at`; many-to-one back-reference to `User`  \n   - Uses SQLAlchemy 2.0 `Mapped` + `mapped_column` typed annotations throughout  \n   - `server_default=func.now()` for DB-side timestamp defaults\n\n4. **`team-test/database/seed_data.py`**  \n   - 3 seed users (alice, bob, charlie) with SHA-256 hashed passwords  \n   - 4 seed projects distributed across the users  \n   - `seed(db=None)` function accepts an optional session (testable) or creates its own  \n   - Idempotent: skips if users already exist  \n   - `db.flush()` before projects to get user IDs without committing  \n   - Proper rollback on error; `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` entry point  \n   - `sys.path` manipulation for standalone script execution\n\nAll four files pass `python -m py_compile` with zero errors.",
